<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hansome says buying back 20,000 shrs.</title>
<headline>Hansome says buying back 20,000 shrs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hansome Co Ltd said on Thursday it would buy back 20,000 shares of its own stock in the open market between January 13 and April 12 to boost its stock price.  </p>
<p>The buyback, representing 1.38 percent of its outstanding shares, would be handled through Tongyang Securities, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Hansome currently holds none of its common shares, it said.</p>
<p>The statement said buy orders would be based on the previous day's closing price.</p>
<p>Hansome shares closed at 30,000 won on Thursday, up 700 won.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
